# banshee-2dq: the Jetsam dimension bands on an HONEST kill count — only kills
# flagged rf:high / per-process-limit / vm-pageshortage, never the routine
# idle-exit rf:low reaping a healthy machine does constantly. Dropping the
# positive reason filter (count every "memorystatus: killing" line) reads the
# fixture's 6 raw kills instead of its 3 genuine ones — exactly the
# false-positive generator this replaced (the old sysctl lens fired on any
# jetsam). Note the idle-exit guard ABOVE this is belt-and-suspenders and would
# NOT catch this alone: rf:low lines fail the positive filter anyway, so the
# reason filter is the load-bearing line.
file: rust/banshee-core/src/census/mod.rs
test: only_genuine_pressure_kills_are_counted_not_idle_exit_noise
---OLD---
    line.contains("rf:high")
        || line.contains("per-process-limit")
        || line.contains("vm-pageshortage")
---NEW---
    true
